self-test: with all the numbers equal the count is exactly C(m, m div 2) for m = 0 to 8, so statement 1 cannot be improved; exponents 0, 1 on the modulus 2 give 4 = 2 C(2, 1), equality in statement 5
1 real: 3000 cases (0 to 11 numbers, whole, none zero; every value v that any signed sum takes, and one that none takes), none against it; the bound met with equality in 1566
2 complex: 3000 cases (0 to 11 numbers, whole real and imaginary parts, none zero; every value v that any signed sum takes, and one that none takes), none against it; the bound met with equality in 570
3 one divisor: 2500 cases (d in 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 12, 15), none against it; equality in 508
4 odd number of elements, never bad at 1: 1135 cases with m odd, every signing, none bad
5 moduli 2^k: 2500 cases (k 0 to 3), none against it; equality in 564
6 odd number of elements on moduli 2^k: 1135 cases with m odd, every signing, none bad
7 every modulus: 2500 cases (k 0 to 3; n' in 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 15), none against it; equality in 151
